Compression

This also connects to compression.

Imagine an idea as one dense object.

A partition chooses where to place the boundaries.

Different partitions optimize different things:

* memory
* teaching
* persuasion
* computation
* discovery
* action

That’s remarkably close to how good interfaces work—they don’t change the underlying system, they expose a useful partition of it.

